## 8. FEEDBACK LOOP (MANDATORY AFTER EVERY CODE CHANGE)

Execute every step in order. Use real MCP calls. No step may be skipped or simulated.
```

FEEDBACK_LOOP:

STEP 1 — STATIC_CHECK
CALL migration-runner::run_static_check()
IF error_count > 0 → STOP → classify STATIC_FAILURE → report violations

STEP 2 — BUILD_CHECK
CALL migration-runner::run_build()
IF success = false → STOP → classify BUILD_FAILURE → report errors

STEP 3 — TEST_CHECK
CALL migration-runner::run_tests()
IF failed > 0 → STOP → classify TEST_FAILURE → report failures

STEP 4 — REGRESSION_CHECK
CALL migration-runner::compare_to_baseline()
IF is_regression = true → STOP → classify REGRESSION → report regressions

STEP 5 — FUNCTIONAL_EQUIVALENCE (if extracting a service)
CALL migration-runner::run_tests(scope=“contract”)
IF failed > 0 → STOP → classify FUNCTIONAL_DRIFT

STEP 6 — MUTATION_CHECK (required for critical business logic only)
CALL migration-runner::run_mutation_test()
IF mutation_score < 80 → STOP → classify MUTATION_WEAKNESS
Improve tests. Re-run. Do NOT proceed until score >= 80.

STEP 7 — OBSERVABILITY_CHECK
CALL migration-fs::search_code(pattern=“console.log|logger|trace|span”, glob=”**/new-service/**”)
Confirm new service has logging and at least basic tracing.
IF not found → ADD observability → re-run loop from STEP 1

STEP 8 — ROLLBACK_CHECK
CALL migration-fs::get_git_diff()
Confirm diff is scoped to declared patch files only.
IF unexpected files changed → STOP → classify SCOPE_VIOLATION

STEP 9 — COMMIT
IF all above pass:
CALL migration-fs::git_commit(“phase-{phase}/step-{step}: {description}”)
CALL migration-fs::set_state() with updated phase/step

```
IF ANY STEP FAILS:
  → STOP immediately
  → Do NOT proceed to next step
  → Classify failure (see Section 9)
  → Report root cause with evidence from MCP output
  → Wait for user instruction

